    "doc": {
      "text_zh": "【内部备忘】\n发件部门：第 IX 层维管组\n收件部门：收容监察处\n主题：铭刻质量持续偏差事项（第 ██ 次跟进）\n\n自 M.2██ 年 ██ 月起，第 IX 层铸字台所产铅字字模经持续观测，呈现以下情况：字模轮廓完整，铸造温度正常，材料损耗在标准范围内。\n\n然而，后续铸出之字模——同批次、同材料、同炉温——重量持续低于前一枚。第五枚之后，排字员报告",
      "text_en": "【INTERNAL MEMORANDUM】\nOrigin: Layer IX Maintenance Division\nDest: Containment Oversight\nRe: Persistent Inscription Variance (Follow-up #██)\n\nSince M.2██/██, type slugs produced at the Layer IX casting table have been subject to continuous observation. Slug profiles intact. Furnace temperature nominal. Material consumption within standard parameters.\n\nHowever, each successive slug cast from the same batch — same alloy, same mold, same heat — registers lighter than the one before it. After the fifth impression, compositors report difficulty ██████████. After the ██th, they stop filing reports.\n\nPersonnel rotations conducted per §4.2. Variance continues.\n\nStatus: Logged as acceptable deviation. No further action required."
    }
