      "text_zh": "──────────────────────────────\n内部备忘\n主题：第 IV 层铸字台区域——铸出字符异常报告（第 ██ 次跟进）\n编号：M-0██-F017-████ / 发件部门：铸造维护科 / 收件部门：收容事务处\n──────────────────────────────\n\n本备忘为上述编号表单的第 ██ 次提交。现象自 M.2██ 年 ██ 月起持续记录，至今未变。\n\n第 IV 层西段铸字台于例行铸印作业期间，铸出字符中持续夹有非标准符号。符号形态包括但不限于：竖杠、星号、括弧、斜线及无法归类之印记。与标准字模核对后，上述符号均不存在于本层字盘中。\n\n首次记录见于 M.2██-██-██。当日当班键徒 D-████ 提交 F-017 表单，称",
      "text_en": "INTERNAL MEMORANDUM\nSubject: Layer IV Casting Hall — Non-Standard Glyph Output (Follow-up #██)\nRef: M-0██-F017-████ / From: Foundry Maintenance Division / To: Containment Affairs Office\n──────────────────────────────\nThis memorandum constitutes the ██th submission under the above reference number. The phenomenon has been continuously recorded since Month ██ of M.2██. No change in status.\n\nDuring routine impression operations, the casting tables of Layer IV West Wing have persistently produced characters interspersed with non-standard marks. Documented forms include but are not limited to: vertical bars, asterisks, parentheses, oblique strokes, and impressions that resist classification. Cross-referencing against the standard type-case requisition ledger confirms that none of the above marks are present in this layer's compositing frames.\n\nFirst recorded M.2██-██-██. D-████, the Clavigerant on duty, submitted F-017 stating that the cast slugs appeared correct at the moment of impression, but the marks were already present when the tray was lifted. D-████ was replaced under §4.2 before follow-up questioning could be conducted.\n\nSubsequent personnel have submitted materially identical reports. Phrasing varies; content does not.\n\nFoundry Engineering has inspected the casting apparatus on ██ separate occasions. Equipment assessed as: within operational parameters.\n\nPending action: nil. Containment Affairs has not issued a revised handling directive. This office will continue filing follow-up submissions at the standard interval.\n\nAnnex: F-044 records for D-████ through D-████ attached. Forms completed by supervising personnel, per standard procedure."
